¥º∂=◊!ººACïº:∞0<{"title": "EAGON CJ:Eagon CJ is a researcher mentioned in the updated systematic review of bariatric surgery."}{"title": "COLDITZ GA:Colditz GA is a prominent researcher recognized for his contributions to the fields of bariatric surgery, nutritional factors, and dietary patterns. He is a co-author of an updated systematic review that evaluates the effectiveness and risks associated with bariatric surgery. Additionally, Colditz GA has conducted studies focusing on the relationship between nutritional factors and hypertension, as well as exploring various dietary patterns and their implications for health. His work encompasses a broad range of topics related to nutrition and its impact on health outcomes."}{"title": "GASTRECTOMY:Gastrectomy is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of part or all of the stomach. This procedure is often performed as a treatment for obesity and is mentioned in the context of Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols. Following gastrectomy, specific nutritional protocols are necessary to support recovery, highlighting the importance of tailored post-operative care for patients undergoing this surgery."}{"title": "ALLIED HEALTH SCIENCES SECTION AD HOC NUTRITION COMMITTEE:This committee provides guidelines and recommendations for nutritional practices in surgical weight loss patients."}{"title": "ASMBS:The American Society for Metabolic and Bariatric Surgery (ASMBS) is an organization that focuses on the treatment of obesity and related conditions through surgical methods."}{"title": "LAPAROSCOPIC SURGERY:Laparoscopic surgery is a minimally invasive surgical technique that uses small incisions and specialized instruments, often resulting in quicker recovery times."}{"title": "VERY LOW CALORIE DIET (VLCD):VLCD is a dietary regimen that provides very low caloric intake, often used in conjunction with bariatric surgery to promote weight loss."}{"title": "POSTOPERATIVE CARE:Postoperative care involves the management and monitoring of patients after surgery to ensure proper recovery and address any complications."}{"title": "DIEETARY MANAGEMENT:Dietary management refers to the planning and implementation of a diet tailored to meet the specific needs of patients, especially after surgical procedures."}{"title": "DIETARY MANAGEMENT:Dietary management involves adjusting food intake to effectively manage symptoms associated with metabolic disorders, including conditions such as galactosaemia and lactose intolerance. This approach focuses on tailoring dietary choices to alleviate the impact of these disorders on an individual's health and well-being."}{"title": "POSE:POSE (Primary Obesity Surgery Endolumenal) is a procedure suggested for treating obesity before considering bariatric surgery."}{"title": "BAL\u00d3N INTRAG\u00c1STRICO:The intragastric balloon (BIG) is a temporary therapeutic strategy for significant weight loss before bariatric surgery."}{"title": "GASTRECTOM\u00cdA ENDOSC\u00d3PICA (APOLLO):The endoscopic vertical gastrectomy (Apollo) aims to mimic surgical gastrectomy by suturing the stomach internally."}{"title": "ENDOBARRIER:EndoBarrier is a medical device designed for the treatment of obesity and type 2 diabetes, primarily by regulating gastrointestinal hormones. This innovative device, also known as the endoluminal bypass or endobarrier, is strategically placed in the duodenum to inhibit food absorption, thereby enhancing glycemic control in individuals with diabetes. Through its mechanism of action, EndoBarrier aims to provide a non-surgical option for managing these conditions effectively."}{"title": "DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2 (DM2):Type 2 diabetes (DM2) is a chronic condition that affects the way the body processes blood sugar (glucose) and can be improved through weight loss."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N Y SOPORTE METAB\u00d3LICO:"}{"title": "LOPEZ-NAVA G:L\u00f3pez-Nava G is a researcher involved in multiple studies related to obesity surgery and its outcomes."}{"title": "BAUTISTA-CASTA\u00d1O I:Bautista-Casta\u00f1o I is a researcher who co-authored studies on obesity surgery and its effects on patients."}{"title": "JIMENEZ A:Jimenez A is a researcher contributing to studies on the safety and outcomes of obesity surgery."}{"title": "DE GRADO T:de Grado T is a researcher involved in obesity surgery studies, focusing on patient outcomes."}{"title": "FERNANDEZ-CORBELLE JP:Fernandez-Corbelle JP is a researcher who has co-authored studies on obesity surgery."}{"title": "PRIMARY OBESITY SURGERY ENDOLUMENAL (POSE):The POSE procedure is a surgical technique aimed at weight loss and improving metabolic conditions in patients with obesity."}{"title": "BIOENTERICS INTRAGASTRIC BALLOON (BIB):The BioEnterics Intragastric Balloon is a device used in obesity treatment, focusing on weight loss and patient management."}{"title": "ENDOSCOPIC SLEEVE GASTROPLASTY:Endoscopic Sleeve Gastroplasty is a minimally invasive procedure for weight loss and management of obesity-related conditions."}{"title": "HEMOGLOBIN A1C:Hemoglobin A1C is a blood test that measures average blood sugar levels over the past 2 to 3 months, commonly used to monitor diabetes control."}{"title": "GASTRECTOMY TUBULAR:Gastrectomy tubular is a surgical procedure that involves removing a portion of the stomach to aid in weight loss and improve metabolic conditions."}{"title": "COMORBIDITIES:Comorbidities are additional medical conditions that occur alongside a primary condition, such as obesity, which can complicate treatment and outcomes."}{"title": "METAANALYSIS:A meta-analysis is a statistical analysis that combines the results of multiple scientific studies to identify patterns and draw conclusions about a specific topic."}{"title": "RISK OF INFARTO AGUDO DE MIOCARDIO:The risk of acute myocardial infarction refers to the likelihood of experiencing a heart attack, often assessed in studies related to obesity and surgery."}{"title": "EVENTOS CV:Eventos CV refers to cardiovascular events, which include incidents such as heart attacks and strokes, often studied in relation to obesity and surgical outcomes.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "KWOCK CS:Kwok CS is an author of a study published in the International Journal of Cardiology regarding the long-term mortality in patients undergoing bariatric surgery."}{"title": "GALLSTONES:Gallstones are a potential complication that can arise after bariatric surgery, particularly after significant weight loss."}{"title": "FISHER DP:Fisher DP is an author of a study published in JAMA that discusses the association between bariatric surgery and macrovascular disease outcomes in patients with type 2 diabetes and severe obesity."}{"title": "SJ\u00d6STR\u00d6M L:Sj\u00f6str\u00f6m L is a researcher known for their work in the field of obesity treatments. They have authored a study published in JAMA that investigates the long-term cardiovascular events associated with bariatric surgery. Through their research, Sj\u00f6str\u00f6m L contributes valuable insights into the effects of surgical interventions on obesity and related health outcomes."}{"title": "MORAIS M:Morais M is an author of a study published in the World Journal of Surgery discussing gallstones and bariatric surgery."}{"title": "WARSCHKOW R:Warschkow R is an author of a meta-analysis published in Obesity Surgery regarding concomitant cholecystectomy during laparoscopic Roux-en-Y gastric bypass."}{"title": "OBESITY SURGERY:Obesity Surgery is a medical journal that focuses on the publication of multiple studies related to bariatric surgery techniques and their outcomes. The term \"obesity surgery\" encompasses a range of surgical procedures designed for weight loss, including various techniques such as gastric bypass. This field of medicine aims to provide effective solutions for individuals struggling with obesity through surgical interventions."}{"title": "ELIASSON B:"}{"title": "HOSPITAL RAM\u00d3N Y CAJAL:El Hospital Ram\u00f3n y Cajal de Madrid es un centro donde se realiz\u00f3 la especialidad en Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n."}{"title": "HOSPITAL SANTIAGO AP\u00d3STOL:El Hospital Santiago Ap\u00f3stol de Vitoria es donde Francisco Javier Escalada San Mart\u00edn trabaj\u00f3 como adjunto de Endocrinolog\u00eda."}{"title": "HOSPITAL CL\u00cdNICO UNIVERSITARIO LOZANO BLES:The Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario Lozano Blesa is a clinical hospital located in Zaragoza, Spain, known for providing a range of medical services and engaging in research activities. Dr. Julia Oc\u00f3n Bret\u00f3n serves as the head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at this institution. Additionally, Francisco Javier Escalada San Mart\u00edn was associated with the hospital, working there from 2005 to 2007."}{"title": "FRANCISCO JAVIER ESCALADA SAN MART\u00cdN:Francisco Javier Escalada San Mart\u00edn es un m\u00e9dico especializado en Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, director del Departamento de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n de la Cl\u00ednica Universidad de Navarra."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD DE ALCAL\u00c1 DE HENARES:La Universidad de Alcal\u00e1 de Henares es donde Francisco Javier Escalada San Mart\u00edn obtuvo su doctorado en Medicina en 1994."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD DE ZARAGOZA:The Universidad de Zaragoza is an educational institution located in Spain, where Francisco Javier Escalada San Mart\u00edn has served as an associate professor in the field of Health Sciences."}{"title": "OMEPRAZOL:Omeprazol is a medication that the patient is taking to reduce the production of stomach acid. It is commonly used to treat conditions such as gastroesophageal reflux disease. Additionally, Omeprazol can affect the absorption of vitamin B12, particularly in patients who have undergone gastric bypass surgery. The medication's absorption can also be enhanced when the stomach pH is elevated by food. Overall, Omeprazol plays a significant role in managing acid-related disorders while also necessitating consideration of its effects on nutrient absorption."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO CLORH\u00cdDRICO:\u00c1cido clorh\u00eddrico es un compuesto qu\u00edmico esencial en varios procesos biol\u00f3gicos y m\u00e9dicos. En el contexto de la digesti\u00f3n, el \u00e1cido clorh\u00eddrico es necesario para la digesti\u00f3n de alimentos que contienen vitamina B12; su ausencia puede llevar a una deficiencia de esta vitamina crucial. Adem\u00e1s, el \u00e1cido clorh\u00eddrico se utiliza en el \u00e1mbito de la medicina para acidificar muestras de orina, lo que ayuda a prevenir alteraciones en las muestras antes de su procesamiento en pruebas diagn\u00f3sticas."}{"title": "FACTOR INTR\u00cdNSECO:El factor intr\u00ednseco es una prote\u00edna necesaria para la absorci\u00f3n de vitamina B12 en el \u00edleon distal."}{"title": "DEPARTAMENTO DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The Department of Endocrinology and Nutrition at the University Clinic of Navarra focuses on research and education in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD DE NAVARRA:The University of Navarra is an educational institution where the Department of Endocrinology and Nutrition is located, involved in medical education and research."}{"title": "AVANCES EN DIABETOLOG\u00cdA:A journal focused on advancements in diabetes research, where the individual served as an associate editor."}{"title": "ENDOCINOLOG\u00cdA, DIABETES Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:A journal where the individual served as deputy editor from April 2017 to April 2019."}{"title": "HIPERCOLESTEROLEMIA FAMILIAR:Hipercolesterolemia Familiar is a genetic disorder characterized by significantly elevated cholesterol levels, particularly high levels of low-density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol. This condition is primarily caused by mutations in the LDL receptor, which results in high cholesterol levels from birth. The disorder occurs with a frequency of approximately one individual per million and is associated with plasma cholesterol levels exceeding 500 mg/dl. Due to its implications for cardiovascular health, Hipercolesterolemia Familiar is a major focus of research within the field of endocrinology, as it often leads to serious cardiovascular events."}{"title": "CELULAS MESENQUIMALES:Mesenchymal cells are a focus of research in diabetes treatment, particularly in relation to type 1 diabetes."}{"title": "PROYECTOS DE INVESTIGACI\u00d3N:Research projects related to diabetes are a key aspect of Samuel Namara's work as a principal investigator."}{"title": "JUNTA DE LA SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The board of the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition oversees educational programs for residents and continuing education for specialists."}{"title": "GRUPOS DE TRABAJO DE DIABETES:Working groups on diabetes within the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition focus on advancing knowledge and treatment of diabetes."}{"title": "GRUPO DE CONSENSOS DE LA SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE DIABETES:A consensus group within the Spanish Diabetes Society that works on guidelines and best practices for diabetes management."}{"title": "GRUPO DE L\u00cdPIDOS DE LA SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:A working group focused on lipid disorders within the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition."}{"title": "HIPERCOLESTEROLEMIA POLIG\u00c9NICA:Hipercolesterolemia polig\u00e9nica is a common condition characterized by moderate levels of cholesterol in the plasma, typically ranging between 240 and 350 mg/dl. This condition arises from the interaction of multiple genetic factors and environmental influences, leading to elevated cholesterol levels."}{"title": "DEFICIT FAMILIAR DE APOPROTE\u00cdNA B-100:Este trastorno autos\u00f3mico dominante es una fenocopia de la hipercolesterolemia familiar, causado por una mutaci\u00f3n que afecta la afinidad de la LDL por su receptor."}{"title": "EZETIMIBA:Ezetimiba is a medication that can be added to statins to help achieve LDL cholesterol goals. It works by inhibiting the absorption of cholesterol and phytosterols in the intestine, making it primarily effective in lowering LDL cholesterol levels."}{"title": "INHIBIDORES DE PCSK9:Los inhibidores de PCSK9 son una clase de medicamentos que ayudan a reducir los niveles de colesterol LDL en pacientes que no logran el control adecuado con estatinas."}{"title": "ALIROCUMAB:Alirocumab es un inhibidor de PCSK9 utilizado para el tratamiento de la hipercolesterolemia."}{"title": "SENSIBILIDAD A LA INSULINA:La sensibilidad a la insulina se refiere a la capacidad del cuerpo para responder a la insulina, y su disminuci\u00f3n est\u00e1 relacionada con la dislipidemia aterog\u00e9nica."}{"title": "CARDIOVASCULAR ENFERMEDAD:"}{"title": "CARDONA F:Cardona F is recognized as one of the authors of the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n,\" a significant contribution to the fields of endocrinology and nutrition. This manual was published by the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, highlighting Cardona F's involvement in advancing knowledge in these areas. Additionally, Cardona F is referenced in the manual, further establishing their role and expertise in the subject matter."}{"title": "ALCAIDE J:Alcaide J is a co-author of the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n,\" which is published by the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n. This manual serves as a significant resource in the fields of endocrinology and nutrition, and Alcaide J is actively involved in research and the development of guidelines within these disciplines. Additionally, Alcaide J is recognized as one of the authors referenced in this important manual, highlighting their contribution to the literature on endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "FERN\u00c1NDEZ GARC\u00cdA JC:Fern\u00e1ndez Garc\u00eda JC is a notable contributor to the field of endocrinology and nutrition, recognized as one of the authors of the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n.\" This manual, published by the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, showcases the expertise of Fern\u00e1ndez Garc\u00eda JC alongside other contributors. His work is referenced within the manual, highlighting his significant role in advancing knowledge in this specialized area of medicine."}{"title": "HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA FAMILIAR:Hipertrigliceridemia familiar is a genetic disorder characterized by elevated triglyceride levels in the blood. This condition is transmitted as an autosomal dominant trait, meaning that it can be inherited from just one affected parent."}{"title": "HIPERLIPIDEMIA FAMILIAR COMBINADA:\"Hiperlipidemia familiar combinada\" es un trastorno gen\u00e9tico que afecta entre el 0,5% y el 1% de la poblaci\u00f3n norteamericana. Se caracteriza por una captaci\u00f3n reducida de \u00e1cidos grasos libres y una sobreproducci\u00f3n de apolipoprote\u00edna B y triglic\u00e9ridos, manifest\u00e1ndose en forma de lipoprote\u00ednas de muy baja densidad. Esta condici\u00f3n se hereda de manera autos\u00f3mica dominante y se asocia con niveles elevados de l\u00edpidos en la sangre, incluyendo hipertrigliceridemia y colesterol elevado. Adem\u00e1s, puede presentarse como una hiperlipidemia mixta, que puede incluir hipertrigliceridemia aislada o niveles elevados de colesterol. La hiperlipidemia familiar combinada est\u00e1 relacionada con un alto riesgo cardiovascular, lo que la convierte en una preocupaci\u00f3n significativa para la salud de quienes la padecen."}{"title": "XANTOMAS TENDINOSOS:Xantomas tendinosos are cholesterol deposits that can occur in tendons, often associated with certain types of hyperlipidemia."}{"title": "ARCO CORNEAL:Arco corneal refers to a ring around the cornea that can indicate high cholesterol levels, often seen in hyperlipidemia conditions."}{"title": "APOLIPOPROTE\u00cdNA E:La apolipoprote\u00edna E es una prote\u00edna crucial en el catabolismo de los quilomicrones y restos de VLDL, con diferentes genotipos que afectan la dislipidemia."}{"title": "DISBETALIPOPROTEINEMIA:Disbetalipoproteinemia is a rare lipid disorder primarily caused by homozygosity in the apolipoprotein E (apo E) gene. This condition is characterized by a mutation in the apo E gene, which significantly affects the metabolism of lipoproteins. As a result, individuals with disbetalipoproteinemia exhibit elevated levels of triglycerides and very low-density lipoprotein (VLDL) cholesterol, as well as the presence of chylomicrons in fasting states."}{"title": "XANTOMAS:Xantomas are fatty deposits that can form on the skin and are indicative of lipid disorders, such as hypertriglyceridemia and dyslipidemia. These deposits are often associated with metabolic disorders and can occur in individuals with high cholesterol levels, particularly in cases of familial hypercholesterolemia and dysbetalipoproteinemia. Overall, xantomas serve as a manifestation of underlying lipid abnormalities in affected patients."}{"title": "LIPOPROTE\u00cdNAS DE MUY BAJA DENSIDAD:Las lipoprote\u00ednas de muy baja densidad (VLDL) son un tipo de lipoprote\u00edna que se produce en el h\u00edgado y est\u00e1 asociada con el transporte de triglic\u00e9ridos en la sangre."}{"title": "APOLIPOPROTE\u00cdNA B:La apolipoprote\u00edna B es una prote\u00edna que se asocia con lipoprote\u00ednas y es un marcador importante en el diagn\u00f3stico de dislipidemias."}{"title": "LIPID DISORDERS:Lipid disorders refer to abnormalities in lipid metabolism, which can result in conditions such as hyperlipidemia and are often managed through dietary changes and medications."}{"title": "CHOLESTEROL:Cholesterol is a lipid that serves as an important indicator of nutritional status and overall health. It is a waxy substance found in the blood, essential for building cells. However, while cholesterol is necessary for various bodily functions, high levels can lead to significant health issues, including heart disease."}{"title": "HYPERLIPIDEMIA:Hyperlipidemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of lipids in the blood. This condition poses significant health risks, particularly increasing the likelihood of cardiovascular diseases. It is especially concerning for patients receiving intravenous lipids and those who have undergone liver transplantation. Management of hyperlipidemia can often be achieved through dietary changes, as supported by various studies."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD EUROPEA DE CARDIOLOG\u00cdA:The European Society of Cardiology is an organization that provides guidelines for cardiovascular disease prevention and treatment."}{"title": "AMOR FERN\u00c1NDEZ AJ:Amor Fern\u00e1ndez AJ is an author of the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n.\" This manual addresses various topics in the field of endocrinology and nutrition, including the treatment of dyslipidemias."}{"title": "VINAGRE TORRES I:Vinagre Torres I is an author of the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n.\" This manual addresses various topics in the field of endocrinology and nutrition, including the treatment of dyslipidemias."}{"title": "PEREA CASTILLA V:Perea Castilla V is an author of the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n,\" a comprehensive guide that addresses various aspects of endocrinology and nutrition. This manual specifically includes discussions on the treatment of dyslipidemias, highlighting Perea Castilla V's contributions to the field."}{"title": "FILTRADO GLOMERULAR ESTIMADO:The estimated glomerular filtration rate is a test used to assess kidney function and is referenced in cardiovascular risk assessment."}{"title": "RIESGO MUY ALTO:A classification group defined by the European Society of Cardiology for patients with a very high risk of cardiovascular events."}{"title": "RIESGO ALTO:A classification group defined by the European Society of Cardiology for patients with a high risk of cardiovascular events."}{"title": "AMOR FERN\u00c1NDEZ:Amor Fern\u00e1ndez is an author known for the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n,\" a significant work that addresses treatments for dyslipidemia and contributes to the broader field of endocrinology and nutrition. Through this manual, Fern\u00e1ndez provides valuable insights and guidance on managing dyslipidemias, highlighting the importance of nutrition in endocrine health."}{"title": "VINAGRE TORRES:Vinagre Torres is an author of the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n,\" where he has made significant contributions to the field of endocrinology and nutrition. Specifically, he has contributed to the chapter on dyslipidemias, which plays a crucial role in the treatment of dyslipidemia. Through his work, Vinagre Torres has enhanced the understanding and management of this important health issue."}{"title": "PEREA CASTILLA:Perea Castilla is an accomplished author of the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n,\" which emphasizes the importance of endocrinology and nutrition in medical practice. Specifically, Perea Castilla focuses on the treatment of dyslipidemias, contributing valuable insights and knowledge to this area of study. Through this manual, Perea Castilla aims to enhance understanding and management of dyslipidemia, thereby advancing the field of endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "INFARTO DE MIOCARDIO:Infarto de miocardio, or myocardial infarction, is a serious cardiovascular event that can occur due to high cholesterol levels."}{"title": "HOMBRE DE 34 A\u00d1OS:A 34-year-old man referred for consultation due to persistently high LDL cholesterol levels."}{"title": "COLESTEROL LDL:"}{"title": "APO B DEFECTUOSA FAMILIAR:Apo B defectuosa familiar is an autosomal dominant disorder that mimics hypercholesterolemia familiar due to a mutation affecting LDL receptor affinity."}{"title": "SITOSTEROLEMIA:Sitosterolemia is a rare lipid metabolism disorder resulting in the accumulation of plant sterols in the blood due to defective intestinal and hepatic excretion."}{"title": "HYPERCHOLESTEROLEMIA FAMILIAR:"}{"title": "QUILOMICRONES:QUILOMICRONES are large lipoprotein particles that originate in the intestine and are primarily composed of triglycerides. They play a crucial role in the transport of dietary lipids, including triglycerides and other fats, from the intestines to various tissues throughout the body. Additionally, quilomicrones can be involved in conditions such as hyperlipidemia, which is characterized by elevated levels of lipids in the blood. Overall, quilomicrones are essential for lipid transport and metabolism within the body."}{"title": "APO B-100:Apolipoprotein B-100 (Apo B-100) is a crucial protein involved in the metabolism of low-density lipoprotein (LDL) and is recognized by LDL receptors. It serves as the primary apolipoprotein of LDL, playing a vital role in lipid metabolism and transport."}{"title": "APO B-48:Apolipoprotein B-48 is the main apolipoprotein of VLDL, crucial for the metabolism of lipoproteins."}{"title": "LIPOPROTEINA LIPASA (LPL):Lipoprotein lipase (LPL) is an enzyme that hydrolyzes triglycerides in lipoproteins, facilitating the release of free fatty acids to tissues."}{"title": "TEJIDO ADIPOSO:TEJIDO ADIPOSO, or adipose tissue, is a type of connective tissue that serves as a crucial storage site for fat, playing a significant role in energy metabolism. It is involved in the storage and metabolism of energy, with its functions being influenced by the gut microbiota and various signaling molecules. Adipose tissue receives fatty acids released from lipoproteins, further contributing to its role in lipid storage and overall energy balance in the body."}{"title": "MUSCULO ESQUELETICO:Skeletal muscle is a site of utilization for fatty acids released from lipoproteins."}{"title": "IDLS:Intermediate-density lipoproteins (IDLs) are formed during the metabolism of VLDL and are involved in lipid transport."}{"title": "LDLS:Low-density lipoproteins (LDLs) are the final product of the VLDL-IDL-LDL metabolic cascade, primarily transporting cholesterol to cells."}{"title": "HDLS:High-density lipoproteins (HDLs) are involved in reverse cholesterol transport and are synthesized from the catabolism of VLDL."}{"title": "VLDL:VLDL, or Very Low-Density Lipoprotein, are a type of lipoprotein produced by the liver. They play a crucial role in lipid metabolism by transporting triglycerides and cholesterol from the liver to various tissues in the body. VLDL is particularly associated with conditions such as combined familial hyperlipidemia, which is characterized by elevated levels of lipids in the blood. Overall, VLDL are essential for the distribution of lipids throughout the body, facilitating the delivery of energy and structural components to cells."}{"title": "APOLIPOPROTEINAS:Apolipoproteins are proteins that bind lipids to form lipoproteins, playing critical roles in lipid metabolism."}{"title": "TRIGLICERIDOS:Trigliceridos, also known as triglycerides, are a type of fat found in the blood that play a crucial role in energy storage and metabolism. They are the main type of fat in the body and serve as a significant energy source, as well as being a component of lipid solutions and lipoproteins. The levels of triglycerides are particularly important to monitor in patients receiving lipid infusions during parenteral nutrition, highlighting their relevance in clinical settings. Overall, triglycerides are essential for various bodily functions, including energy provision and the formation of important biological molecules."}{"title": "LIPOPROTEINAS:"}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO NICOT\u00cdNICO:\u00c1cido nicot\u00ednico, also known as nicotinic acid, is a medication that has been utilized for over 40 years in the treatment of dyslipidemia. It primarily functions by decreasing the production and release of very low-density lipoprotein (VLDL), which is crucial for managing lipid levels in the body. Additionally, nicotinic acid can be used in conjunction with fibrates to effectively lower triglyceride levels, further supporting its role in lipid management."}{"title": "MANUAL DE NUTRICI\u00d3N:The Manual de Nutrici\u00f3n is a publication that includes guidelines and information on nutrition and metabolism, published by the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n."}{"title": "AACE/ACE:The AACE/ACE refers to the American Association of Clinical Endocrinology and the American College of Endocrinology, organizations that provide guidelines for managing dyslipidemia and cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "HMG-COA REDUCTASA:HMG-CoA reductase is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in cholesterol biosynthesis and is the target of statin medications."}{"title": "HIPERLIPIDEMIA:Hiperlipidemia refers to elevated levels of lipids in the blood, which is a condition treated with various medications including statins and fibrates."}{"title": "HYPERTRIGLYCERIDEMIA:HYPERTRIGLYCERIDEMIA is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of triglycerides in the blood. This condition can pose significant health risks, including an increased likelihood of pancreatitis and cardiovascular issues. Management of hypertriglyceridemia can be achieved through dietary supplementation, including the use of medium-chain triglycerides (MCTs), which may help improve triglyceride levels. Overall, hypertriglyceridemia is associated with various health complications, making its management important for maintaining overall health."}{"title": "LIPOPROTE\u00cdNA LIPASA:Lipoprote\u00edna lipasa is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in lipid metabolism, specifically in the breakdown of triglycerides. It facilitates the hydrolysis of triglycerides in lipoproteins such as chylomicrons and very low-density lipoproteins (VLDL). This enzyme is essential for the metabolism of triglycerides and is involved in the processing of lipoproteins in the bloodstream, highlighting its importance in maintaining lipid homeostasis."}{"title": "CITOCROMO P450:Cytochrome P450 is a family of enzymes that play a crucial role in the metabolism of a wide variety of drugs, including statins, which can influence their efficacy and safety. These enzymes are primarily located in the liver, where they facilitate the metabolic processes necessary for drug processing and elimination from the body."}{"title": "MIALGIAS:Myalgias refer to muscle pain that can occur as a side effect of statin use, often without elevated creatine kinase levels."}{"title": "MIOPAT\u00cdA:MIOPAT\u00cdA refers to a condition characterized by muscle weakness and pain, which can manifest as a result of various underlying issues, including disorders related to the \u03b2-oxidation of fatty acids. Additionally, myopathy can occur as a side effect of statin medications, which are commonly used to lower cholesterol levels. This condition highlights the importance of understanding the different causes and implications of muscle-related diseases."}{"title": "APO C-II:Apolipoprotein C-II (Apo C-II) is a crucial cofactor that plays an essential role in the activation of lipoprotein lipase. This protein associates with lipoproteins and is vital for the metabolism of triglycerides, facilitating the breakdown and utilization of these fats in the body."}{"title": "HEPATOMEGALIA:Hepatomegalia is a clinical condition characterized by the enlargement of the liver. This condition can manifest as a result of various metabolic disorders, including a deficiency in lipoprotein lipase. It is commonly associated with glycogen storage diseases (GSD), particularly GSDIII, and can be observed in children suffering from these conditions. Additionally, hepatomegalia may also be a symptom of Wilson's disease, highlighting its relevance in a range of hepatic disorders. Overall, hepatomegalia serves as an important clinical indicator of underlying metabolic issues affecting liver function."}{"title": "ESPLENOMEGALIA:Esplenomegalia, tambi\u00e9n conocida como agrandamiento del bazo, es una condici\u00f3n que puede estar asociada con trastornos metab\u00f3licos y la acumulaci\u00f3n de l\u00edpidos en el cuerpo. Esta afecci\u00f3n puede desarrollarse en adultos que est\u00e1n recibiendo tratamiento con factores estimulantes de colonias, lo que puede afectar su salud."}{"title": "DISLIPIDEMIAS:Las dislipidemias son trastornos que afectan los niveles de l\u00edpidos en la sangre, incluyendo hipertrigliceridemia y otros desequilibrios lip\u00eddicos."}{"title": "QUILOMICRONEMIA:La quilomicronemia es una condici\u00f3n caracterizada por niveles elevados de quilomicrones en la sangre, a menudo debido a un d\u00e9ficit de lipoprote\u00edna lipasa."}{"title": "APO V:Apolipoprote\u00edna V es una prote\u00edna que se asocia con lipoprote\u00ednas y tiene un papel en la uni\u00f3n de VLDL y quilomicrones con lipoprote\u00edna lipasa."}{"title": "OREA SOLER I:Orea Soler I is an author of the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, which discusses lipid metabolism in healthy individuals."}{"title": "ILL\u00c1N G\u00d3MEZ F:Ill\u00e1n G\u00f3mez F is a co-author of the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, contributing to the chapter on lipid metabolism."}{"title": "LIPASA:LIPASA is an enzyme that plays a vital role in lipid metabolism by catalyzing the hydrolysis of fats. It is essential for breaking down fats in the digestive system, making it particularly important for individuals with conditions such as cystic fibrosis, where it is often included in pancreatic enzyme preparations to aid digestion."}{"title": "IDL:IDL (Intermediate-Density Lipoprotein) are lipoproteins that are formed from the metabolism of VLDL and are involved in cholesterol transport."}{"title": "LDL:LDL (Low-Density Lipoprotein) are the final product of the metabolic cascade VLDL-IDL-LDL, primarily responsible for transporting cholesterol to cells."}{"title": "LPL:Lipoprotein Lipase (LPL) is an enzyme that hydrolyzes triglycerides in lipoproteins, facilitating the release of free fatty acids for tissue use and storage."}{"title": "APO E:Apolipoprotein E (Apo E) is a protein involved in the clearance of lipoproteins from the bloodstream, particularly in the metabolism of IDL and chylomicron remnants."}{"title": "PCSK9:Proprotein Convertase Subtilisin/Kexin Type 9 (PCSK9) is a protein that regulates LDL receptor levels and is involved in cholesterol metabolism."}{"title": "DIETA DASH:The DASH (Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension) diet is a dietary plan aimed at reducing hypertension and improving overall health, which may also affect lipid levels."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS POLIINSATURADOS:\u00c1cidos grasos poliinsaturados are essential fats that play a significant role in promoting cardiovascular health. These fats, which include omega-3 and omega-6 fatty acids, are found in various food sources and are recognized for their beneficial effects on heart health. Dietary guidelines recommend the inclusion of polyunsaturated fatty acids in moderation as part of a healthy diet, highlighting their importance in maintaining overall well-being."}{"title": "HIDROLIZADAS:The process of hydrolysis refers to the breakdown of triglycerides in lipoproteins by enzymes such as LPL."}{"title": "SOCIETAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE ARTERIOSCLEROSIS:The \"Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Arteriosclerosis\" is an organization dedicated to promoting cardiovascular health through the establishment of dietary recommendations. It provides guidelines and classifications for foods, specifically focusing on their impact on lipid levels. This dual approach emphasizes the importance of nutrition in managing and preventing atherosclerosis and related cardiovascular conditions."}{"title": "PREDIMED:PREDIMED is a large-scale clinical trial conducted in Spain that investigates the effects of the Mediterranean diet, particularly one enriched with olive oil and nuts, on cardiovascular health and other health outcomes. The study involves 7,447 subjects and focuses on the impact of this diet on cardiovascular disease, diabetes, and other chronic conditions. PREDIMED evaluates adherence to the Mediterranean diet through specific questionnaires and dietary history assessments. It also observes the consumption of more than 500 mg of EPA-DHA to assess its benefits on heart attacks and mortality. Additionally, the study highlights the advantages of virgin olive oil and nut fats within the Mediterranean diet for the prevention of cardiovascular events. Overall, PREDIMED aims to demonstrate the health benefits associated with the Mediterranean diet, particularly for individuals at risk for diabetes and cardiovascular diseases."}{"title": "EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF CARDIOLOGY:The European Society of Cardiology (ESC) is a professional organization dedicated to the management and reduction of cardiovascular diseases in Europe. It provides comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for the treatment of various cardiovascular conditions, including dyslipidemia. The ESC focuses on enhancing education and promoting research to address the burden of cardiovascular diseases across the continent. Through its initiatives, the organization aims to improve patient outcomes and advance the field of cardiology."}{"title": "EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF ATHEROSCLEROSIS:The European Society of Atherosclerosis is a professional organization focused on the study and treatment of atherosclerosis and related cardiovascular conditions."}{"title": "HIPERLIPIDEMIA COMBINADA:Hiperlipidemia combinada is a condition involving elevated levels of different types of lipids in the blood, often requiring treatment with medications like statins."}{"title": "GRASAS TRANS:GRASAS TRANS, or trans fats, are a type of fat that is generally avoided in the Mediterranean diet due to their harmful effects on health. These fats have been linked to an increased risk of cardiovascular diseases and other health issues. Dietary guidelines recommend avoiding trans fats because of their negative impact on heart health."}{"title": "CARDIOVASCULAR SALUD:"}{"title": "GRAHAM I:Graham I es uno de los autores de las gu\u00edas de la ESC/EAS 2016 para el manejo de dislipidemias, que se citan en el documento."}{"title": "DE BACKER G:De Backer G es uno de los autores de las gu\u00edas de la ESC/EAS 2016 para el manejo de dislipidemias, que se citan en el documento."}{"title": "WIKLUND O:Wiklund O es uno de los autores de las gu\u00edas de la ESC/EAS 2016 para el manejo de dislipidemias, que se citan en el documento."}{"title": "CHAPMAN MJ:Chapman MJ es uno de los autores de las gu\u00edas de la ESC/EAS 2016 para el manejo de dislipidemias, que se citan en el documento."}{"title": "DREXEL H:Drexel H es uno de los autores de las gu\u00edas de la ESC/EAS 2016 para el manejo de dislipidemias, que se citan en el documento."}{"title": "EUROPEAN ATHEROSCLEROSIS SOCIETY:La European Atherosclerosis Society (EAS) es una organizaci\u00f3n que colabora con la ESC en la elaboraci\u00f3n de gu\u00edas para el manejo de dislipidemias."}{"title": "CATAPANO AL:"}{"title": "FRAMINGHAM:The Framingham study is a long-term, ongoing cardiovascular cohort study conducted among residents of Framingham, Massachusetts. This study has been instrumental in providing significant data on the prevalence of hypertension and its associated risk factors. One of the notable findings from the Framingham study is that individuals with high levels of omega-3 in their blood have a lower incidence of dementia after a follow-up period of nine years. Additionally, the Framingham tables serve as valuable tools for the stratification of cardiovascular risk in patients, utilizing epidemiological data to assess and categorize risk levels effectively."}{"title": "RENAL CR\u00d3NICA:La enfermedad renal cr\u00f3nica es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que implica la p\u00e9rdida gradual de la funci\u00f3n renal y se asocia con un alto riesgo cardiovascular."}{"title": "POLIMORFISMOS DE LIPOPROTE\u00cdNA LIPASA:Los polimorfismos de la lipoprote\u00edna lipasa son variaciones gen\u00e9ticas que pueden influir en el metabolismo de los l\u00edpidos y est\u00e1n relacionados con la hiperlipidemia familiar combinada."}{"title": "APO A-I, APO C-III, APO A-IV:Las apolipoprote\u00ednas A-I, C-III y A-IV son prote\u00ednas que desempe\u00f1an un papel crucial en el metabolismo de los l\u00edpidos y pueden estar implicadas en la hiperlipidemia familiar combinada."}{"title": "FENOTIPO I DE FRIEDRIKS\u00d6N:El fenotipo I de Friedriks\u00f6n se refiere a una forma de hiperlipidemia caracterizada por la presencia de hiperlipidemia primaria, que puede ser relevante en el diagn\u00f3stico diferencial."}{"title": "FENOTIPO IIB DE FRIEDRIKS\u00d6N:El fenotipo IIb de Friedriks\u00f6n se refiere a una forma de hiperlipidemia familiar combinada, que se caracteriza por niveles elevados de colesterol LDL y triglic\u00e9ridos."}{"title": "FENOTIPO III DE FRIEDRIKS\u00d6N:El fenotipo III de Friedriks\u00f6n se refiere a la disbetalipoproteinemia, que es un tipo de trastorno lip\u00eddico que puede ser confundido con la hiperlipidemia familiar combinada."}{"title": "FENOTIPO IV DE FRIEDRIKS\u00d6N:El fenotipo IV de Friedriks\u00f6n se refiere a la hipertrigliceridemia familiar, que es otra forma de trastorno lip\u00eddico que puede coexistir con la hiperlipidemia familiar combinada."}{"title": "LIPASA PANCRE\u00c1TICA:LIPASA PANCRE\u00c1TICA es una enzima que desempe\u00f1a un papel crucial en la digesti\u00f3n de los triglic\u00e9ridos en el intestino delgado. Su funci\u00f3n principal es descomponer estos l\u00edpidos, lo que facilita su absorci\u00f3n en el organismo."}{"title": "LIPIDEMIA RETINALIS:La lipidemia retinalis es una condici\u00f3n ocular que se presenta con la hiperquilomicronemia, caracterizada por un aspecto rosado blanquecino de los vasos retinianos."}{"title": "PANCREATITIS LIP\u00c9MICA:Pancreatitis lip\u00e9mica is a type of pancreatitis characterized by inflammation of the pancreas, which can occur due to the accumulation of chylomicrons and non-esterified fatty acids in the bloodstream. This condition is specifically linked to elevated levels of triglycerides in the blood, which contribute to the inflammatory process."}{"title": "DEFICIT FAMILIAR DE LIPOPROTE\u00cdNA LIPASA:El d\u00e9ficit familiar de lipoprote\u00edna lipasa es un trastorno gen\u00e9tico que causa acumulaci\u00f3n de quilomicrones en el plasma, resultando en hipertrigliceridemia."}{"title": "DEFICIT DE APO C-II:El d\u00e9ficit de apo C-II es un trastorno autos\u00f3mico recesivo que afecta la funci\u00f3n de la lipoprote\u00edna lipasa, causando acumulaci\u00f3n de lipoprote\u00ednas en la sangre."}{"title": "DEFICIT DE LIPASA HEP\u00c1TICA:El d\u00e9ficit de lipasa hep\u00e1tica es un trastorno raro que interfiere con el metabolismo de las lipoprote\u00ednas, contribuyendo a la hipertrigliceridemia."}{"title": "DEFICIT DE APO-V:El d\u00e9ficit de apo-V es un trastorno que afecta la uni\u00f3n de lipoprote\u00ednas a la lipoprote\u00edna lipasa, lo que puede llevar a quilomicronemia."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT FAMILIAR DE LIPOPROTE\u00cdNA LIPASA:El d\u00e9ficit familiar de lipoprote\u00edna lipasa es un trastorno autos\u00f3mico recesivo que causa acumulaci\u00f3n de quilomicrones en el plasma, resultando en hipertrigliceridemia y manifestaciones como xantomas y hepatomegalia."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT DE APO C-II:El d\u00e9ficit de apo C-II es un trastorno autos\u00f3mico recesivo que causa un d\u00e9ficit funcional de la lipoprote\u00edna lipasa, lo que lleva a la acumulaci\u00f3n de quilomicrones y a niveles elevados de triglic\u00e9ridos."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT DE LIPASA HEP\u00c1TICA:El d\u00e9ficit de lipasa hep\u00e1tica es un trastorno autos\u00f3mico recesivo raro que interfiere con el catabolismo de las VLDL e IDL, contribuyendo a la hipertrigliceridemia."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT DE APO-V:El d\u00e9ficit de apo-V es un trastorno que afecta la uni\u00f3n de las VLDL y los quilomicrones con la lipoprote\u00edna lipasa, lo que puede resultar en quilomicronemia."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE MEDICINA INTERNA:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Medicina Interna, also known as the Spanish Society of Internal Medicine, is a prominent medical society in Spain dedicated to the field of internal medicine. This organization plays a crucial role in coordinating medical protocols and guidelines within the country. Among its contributions, the society has published protocols specifically addressing hypertriglyceridemia, which are referenced in various medical texts. Through its efforts, the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Medicina Interna aims to enhance the quality of care and standardize practices in internal medicine across Spain."}{"title": "FENOFIBRATO:Fenofibrate is a medication primarily used to lower triglyceride levels in patients suffering from hypertriglyceridemia. Additionally, it is effective in reducing cholesterol levels and triglycerides in the blood, making it a common prescription for individuals with metabolic disorders."}{"title": "LOMITAPIDA:Lomitapide is a medication that can be prescribed for severe cases of hypertriglyceridemia."}{"title": "PLASMAF\u00c9RESIS:Plasmapheresis is a medical procedure that is effective in rapidly normalizing triglyceride levels in patients experiencing severe hypertriglyceridemia and pancreatitis. It is particularly useful in acute situations where there is a need to quickly reduce triglyceride levels."}{"title": "H\u00c1BITOS DE VIDA:Lifestyle habits refer to the daily behaviors and practices that can affect health, including diet and exercise."}{"title": "QUILOMICRONEMIAS:"}{"title": "MART\u00cdN CUESTA HERN\u00c1NDEZ:Mart\u00edn Cuesta Hern\u00e1ndez is a licensed physician and endocrinologist with a specialization in diabetes and new technologies. He has a robust background in both research and clinical practice, having worked in Madrid and Dublin. Currently, he serves as an attending physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Cl\u00ednico San Carlos in Madrid."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD AUT\u00d3NOMA DE MADRID:The Universidad Aut\u00f3noma de Madrid is an educational institution where Mart\u00edn Cuesta Hern\u00e1ndez obtained his medical degree in 2009."}{"title": "BEAUMONT HOSPITAL:Beaumont Hospital is a hospital in Dublin where Mart\u00edn Cuesta Hern\u00e1ndez worked as a research registrar in endocrinology."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE QUILOMICRONEMIA:Syndrome of chylomicronemia is a condition referenced in the protocols on hypertriglyceridemia, indicating a specific type of hypertriglyceridemia."}{"title": "URGENCIAS:Urgent care is referenced in the context of a patient presenting with severe symptoms related to electrolyte imbalances."}{"title": "ACIDOSIS TUBULAR PROXIMAL:Proximal tubular acidosis is a condition affecting the kidneys' ability to reabsorb bicarbonate, leading to metabolic acidosis."}{"title": "ACIDOSIS TUBULAR DISTAL:Distal tubular acidosis is a disorder where the kidneys fail to excrete acids into the urine, leading to a buildup of acid in the blood."}{"title": "LACTANTE DE 6 MESES:A 6-month-old infant presenting with dehydration and electrolyte imbalances, indicative of potential underlying health issues."}{"title": "CETOACIDOSIS DIABETICA:Cetoacidosis diab\u00e9tica is a serious complication of diabetes characterized by high levels of ketones in the blood, leading to metabolic acidosis."}{"title": "ACIDOSIS TUBULAR RENAL:La acidosis tubular renal es un cuadro caracterizado por acidosis metab\u00f3lica hiperclor\u00e9mica debido a la incapacidad renal de reabsorber o generar bicarbonato."}{"title": "AVP:Arginine-vasopressin (AVP) is a hormone that plays a crucial role in regulating water retention and osmolarity in the human body. It is particularly significant in the mechanism of nephrogenic diabetes insipidus, a condition characterized by the kidneys' inability to concentrate urine, leading to excessive urination and thirst. AVP helps maintain the balance of water in the body, ensuring proper hydration and physiological function."}{"title": "RADIOTERAPIA HIPOFISARIA:RADIOTERAPIA HIPOFISARIA, or hypophyseal radiotherapy, is a specialized treatment method designed to target pituitary adenomas while minimizing radiation exposure to the surrounding brain structures. This approach is particularly effective in treating these types of tumors without causing adverse effects such as hyponatremia or diabetes insipidus."}{"title": "BESOUW MTP:Besouw MTP es un autor que ha investigado sobre el s\u00edndrome de Bartter y Gitelman."}{"title": "KLETA R:Kleta R es un autor que ha colaborado en investigaciones sobre el s\u00edndrome de Bartter y Gitelman."}{"title": "BOCKENHAUER D:Bockenhauer D es un autor que ha contribuido a la literatura sobre el s\u00edndrome de Bartter y Gitelman."}{"title": "DABROWSKI E:Dabrowski E es un autor que ha investigado sobre la diabetes ins\u00edpida en ni\u00f1os y adolescentes."}{"title": "KADAKIA R:Kadakia R es un autor que ha trabajado en el campo de la diabetes ins\u00edpida en ni\u00f1os y adolescentes."}{"title": "ZIMMERMAN D:Zimmerman D es un autor que ha escrito sobre la diabetes ins\u00edpida en la literatura m\u00e9dica."}{"title": "PELLETIER J:Pelletier J es un autor que ha investigado sobre la acidosis tubular renal."}{"title": "GBADEGESIN R:Gbadegesin R es un autor que ha contribuido a la investigaci\u00f3n sobre la acidosis tubular renal."}{"title": "STAPLES B:Staples B es un autor que ha trabajado en el campo de la acidosis tubular renal."}{"title": "HIPOGLUCEMIA AGUDA:La hiponatremia aguda es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica cr\u00edtica que puede resultar en complicaciones severas como edema cerebral y convulsiones."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE GITELMAN:El s\u00edndrome de Gitelman es un trastorno gen\u00e9tico que afecta la reabsorci\u00f3n de electrolitos en los ri\u00f1ones, similar al s\u00edndrome de Bartter."}{"title": "HIPOCLOROSEMIA:La hipocloremia es una condici\u00f3n caracterizada por niveles bajos de cloro en la sangre, que puede estar asociada con trastornos renales."}{"title": "HORMONAS RENINAS:Las hormonas reninas son enzimas que juegan un papel crucial en la regulaci\u00f3n de la presi\u00f3n arterial y el equilibrio de fluidos en el cuerpo."}{"title": "HORMONAS ADRENALINAS:Las hormonas adrenalinas son hormonas producidas por las gl\u00e1ndulas suprarrenales que ayudan a regular la respuesta del cuerpo al estr\u00e9s.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "\u00c9XTASIS:Ecstasy is a psychoactive drug that can lead to acute hyponatremia due to its effects on water retention and vasopressin release."}{"title": "METANFETAMINA:Methamphetamine is a powerful central nervous system stimulant that can cause severe acute hyponatremia and other health risks."}{"title": "HIPOGLICEMIA AGUDA:Acute hypoglycemia is a rapid drop in blood sugar levels that can lead to symptoms such as confusion, seizures, and loss of consciousness."}{"title": "HIPOGLICEMIA CR\u00d3NICA:Chronic hypoglycemia refers to persistently low blood sugar levels over an extended period, which can have various causes and health implications."}{"title": "NEFROGENICA:Nephrogenic diabetes insipidus is a rare condition where the kidneys fail to respond to antidiuretic hormone, leading to excessive urination and thirst."}{"title": "DIN:Diabetes insipidus nephrogenic (DIN) is a condition characterized by the kidneys' inability to concentrate urine, leading to excessive urination and thirst."}{"title": "HYPERNATREMIA:Hypernatremia is a medical condition characterized by elevated sodium levels in the blood. This condition can arise in various clinical scenarios, including in patients receiving nutritional support, where careful monitoring of sodium levels is essential. Additionally, hypernatremia can occur in individuals with nephrogenic diabetes insipidus, a disorder that affects the kidneys' ability to concentrate urine, leading to increased sodium levels. Overall, hypernatremia necessitates vigilant observation and management to prevent potential complications associated with high sodium concentrations."}{"title": "CIDOFOVIR:Cidofovir is a medication that can cause acquired nephrogenic diabetes insipidus as a side effect."}{"title": "FOSCARNET:Foscarnet is an antiviral medication that can lead to nephrogenic diabetes insipidus in some patients."}{"title": "ANFOTERICINA B:Amphotericin B is an antifungal medication that can cause nephrogenic diabetes insipidus as a side effect."}{"title": "DEMELOCICLINA:Demeclocycline is an antibiotic that can induce nephrogenic diabetes insipidus."}{"title": "IFOSFAMIDA:Ifosfamide is a chemotherapy drug that can lead to nephrogenic diabetes insipidus."}{"title": "OFLOXACINO:Ofloxacin is an antibiotic that can cause nephrogenic diabetes insipidus as a side effect."}{"title": "ORLISTAT:Orlistat is a weight loss medication that has been marketed in Europe since 1998. It functions by inhibiting fat absorption from the diet, making it a popular choice for individuals seeking to lose weight. However, it has been noted that Orlistat has the least effect on body weight compared to other weight loss medications. In clinical trials, Orlistat, also known by its brand name Xenical, has been compared with another weight loss drug, cetilistat. Additionally, it is important to note that Orlistat can lead to nephrogenic diabetes insipidus, a potential side effect associated with its use."}{"title": "GSK3\u0392:Glycogen synthase kinase 3 beta (GSK3\u03b2) is an enzyme involved in cellular signaling pathways that can be inhibited by lithium, affecting aquaporin-2 function."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO CON LITIO:Treatment with lithium is a common approach for mood stabilization but can lead to nephrogenic diabetes insipidus in some patients."}{"title": "OBSTRUCCI\u00d3N BILATERAL DEL TRACTO URINARIO:Bilateral obstruction of the urinary tract can lead to transient nephrogenic diabetes insipidus due to renal cell injury."}{"title": "AQUAPORINA-2:"}{"title": "RUNKLE I:Runkle I is an author known for contributions to the field of clinical gerontology, particularly in the study of hyponatremia. In 2015, Runkle I co-authored a study published in Reviews in Clinical Gerontology that focused on the clinical aspects of hyponatremia. Additionally, Runkle I reported on the use of tolvaptan as a treatment for hyponatremia secondary to the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH). This work highlights Runkle I's involvement in addressing the complexities of hyponatremia and its management in clinical settings."}{"title": "VILLABONA C:Villabona C is one of the authors referenced in the treatment of hyponatremia secondary to the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion."}{"title": "NAVARRO A:Navarro A is one of the authors referenced in the treatment of hyponatremia secondary to the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion."}{"title": "MED CLIN (BARC):Med Clin (Barc) is the journal where the treatment of hyponatremia secondary to the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion was published."}{"title": "OBESIDAD, L\u00cdPIDOS Y TRASTORNOS ELECTROL\u00cdTICOS 8:This refers to a section or chapter discussing obesity, lipids, and electrolyte disorders, particularly focusing on hyponatremia."}{"title": "SYNDROME OF INAPPROPRIATE ANTIDIURETIC HORMONE SECRETION:The syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion is a medical condition that can lead to hyponatremia."}{"title": "HYPONATREMIA:Hyponatremia is a medical condition characterized by abnormally low sodium levels in the blood. This electrolyte imbalance can lead to various health issues, affecting the body's overall function and potentially resulting in serious complications if not addressed."}{"title": "HYPERTONIC SALINE:Hypertonic saline is a concentrated saline solution used to treat severe hyponatremia and reduce cerebral edema."}{"title": "CEREBRAL EDEMA:Cerebral edema is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of excess fluid in the brain. This condition can be induced by hyponatremia, a state of low sodium levels in the blood. The presence of excess fluid can lead to increased intracranial pressure and may require medical intervention to manage the associated risks and complications."}{"title": "SYNDROME OF DESMYELINATION:The syndrome of desmyelination is a potential risk associated with rapid correction of hyponatremia, leading to neurological complications."}{"title": "ELECTROLYTE DISORDERS:Electrolyte disorders refer to imbalances in the body's electrolytes, which can include conditions like hyponatremia."}{"title": "ROTTERDAM STUDY:The Rotterdam Study is a research project that investigates the risk factors for various diseases, including fractures related to mild hyponatremia."}{"title": "HYPO-NATREMIA GUIDELINE DEVELOPMENT GROUP:The Hyponatremia Guideline Development Group is responsible for creating clinical practice guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of hyponatremia."}{"title": "AMERICAN JOURNAL OF MEDICINE:The American Journal of Medicine (Am J Med) is a reputable journal that focuses on publishing research across a diverse array of medical topics. It is particularly noted for its contributions to the understanding and management of hyponatremia, a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood. The journal not only features original research articles but also expert panel recommendations that guide the diagnosis, evaluation, and treatment of hyponatremia. Through its comprehensive coverage, the American Journal of Medicine serves as a valuable resource for medical professionals seeking insights into various health issues, including the complexities surrounding hyponatremia."}{"title": "SPASOVSKI G:Spasovski G is a contributor to the clinical practice guidelines on hyponatremia diagnosis and treatment."}{"title": "VERBALIS JG:Verbalis JG is a prominent researcher and author recognized for his significant contributions to the understanding of hyponatremia and its implications for both diagnosis and therapy. He has conducted extensive research on disorders of body water homeostasis, focusing particularly on the efficacy and safety of conivaptan in patients with euvolemic hyponatremia. Additionally, Verbalis JG has studied the association between moderate hyponatremia and an increased risk of mortality. His expertise has also led him to contribute to the development of recommendations for the diagnosis and treatment of hyponatremia, solidifying his role as a key figure in this field of medical research."}{"title": "FOSTER JE:Foster JE is a researcher who investigated the effects of gentamicin on renal handling of electrolytes."}{"title": "HESS MW:Hess MW is a researcher who conducted a systematic review on hypomagnesemia induced by proton pump inhibition."}{"title": "LAJER H:Lajer H is a researcher who studied magnesium and potassium homeostasis during cisplatin treatment."}{"title": "RYZEN E:Ryzen E is a researcher who examined low intracellular magnesium in patients with acute pancreatitis and hypocalcemia."}{"title": "SHAH GM:Shah GM is a researcher who studied renal magnesium wasting associated with therapeutic agents."}{"title": "WONG ET:Wong ET is a researcher and author who conducted a study on the prevalence of hypomagnesemia and hypermagnesemia in hospitalized patients. In their research, Wong ET reported a high prevalence of both conditions among this patient population, highlighting the significance of monitoring magnesium levels in clinical settings."}{"title": "HYPOPHOSPHATEMIA:Hypophosphatemia is a condition characterized by low levels of phosphate in the blood, which can occur in various clinical situations, including refeeding syndrome."}{"title": "GITELMAN SYNDROME:Gitelman syndrome is a genetic disorder that affects the kidneys' ability to reabsorb certain electrolytes, leading to hypomagnesemia and hypokalemia."}{"title": "BARTTER SYNDROME:Bartter syndrome is a group of rare kidney disorders that result in imbalances of electrolytes, including hypomagnesemia."}{"title": "CISPLATIN:Cisplatin is a chemotherapy drug that can lead to various side effects, including hypomagnesemia and renal toxicity."}{"title": "PROTON PUMP INHIBITORS:Proton pump inhibitors are medications that reduce stomach acid and have been associated with the development of hypomagnesemia."}{"title": "DIURETICS:Diuretics are medications that promote the elimination of water and electrolytes from the body and can lead to hypomagnesemia."}{"title": "ACUTE PANCREATITIS:Acute pancreatitis is a sudden inflammatory condition of the pancreas characterized by severe abdominal pain, necessitating immediate medical attention. This condition can also result in complications such as low intracellular magnesium levels and hypocalcemia, highlighting the potential systemic effects of the inflammation."}{"title": "HYPO-MAGNESEMIA:"}{"title": "FELSENFELD AJ:Felsenfeld AJ is an author who contributed to the treatment of hypophosphatemia in the Am J Kidney Dis journal."}{"title": "LEVIN:Levine BS is an author who contributed to the treatment of hypophosphatemia in the Am J Kidney Dis journal."}{"title": "AM J KIDNEY DIS:Am J Kidney Dis is a medical journal that published research on the treatment of hypophosphatemia."}{"title": "R:R is a section marker in the document, likely indicating a section of answers or responses."}{"title": "RESPUESTAS:Respuestas means \"Answers\" in Spanish, indicating a section of answers in the document."}{"title": "M\u00d3DULO 1:M\u00f3dulo 1 refers to the first module in the document, focusing on the pituitary gland."}{"title": "M\u00d3DULO 2:M\u00f3dulo 2 refers to the second module in the document, focusing on diabetes."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE FANCONI:S\u00edndrome de Fanconi is a disorder that affects the kidneys and can lead to increased phosphate loss, mentioned as a cause of hypophosphatemia."}{"title": "REALIMENTACI\u00d3N:Realimentaci\u00f3n refers to the process of refeeding a patient, which can cause acute movement of phosphate into cells, mentioned in the context of hypophosphatemia."}{"title": "ALCALOSIS RESPIRATORIA:Alcalosis respiratoria is a condition that can influence phosphate levels, particularly in the context of hypophosphatemia. Additionally, it is characterized by an increase in the binding of calcium to albumin, which affects the levels of ionized calcium in the body. This disorder highlights the interconnectedness of electrolyte imbalances and their physiological implications."}{"title": "ANTI\u00c1CIDOS:Anti\u00e1cidos are medications that play a significant role in managing gastrointestinal issues. They can affect phosphate absorption, which is particularly relevant in the context of hypophosphatemia, a condition characterized by low phosphate levels in the blood. Additionally, anti\u00e1cidos can interact with enteral nutrition, potentially leading to gastrointestinal complications. Furthermore, these medications may have interactions with certain nutrients, impacting their absorption. Overall, while anti\u00e1cidos are commonly used to alleviate symptoms related to acidity, their effects on nutrient absorption and gastrointestinal health warrant careful consideration."}{"title": "HIPOCLASIA:Hipoclasia refers to a condition of underdevelopment, mentioned in the context of the effects of hypophosphatemia."}{"title": "HYPERPARATIROIDISMO:Hyperparatiroidismo is a condition that can lead to increased urinary phosphate loss, discussed in the context of hypophosphatemia.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "M\u00d3DULO 3:M\u00f3dulo 3 focuses on the topic of Thyroid, containing a series of questions and answers related to it."}{"title": "B:B is a response option in the context of the questions presented in the modules."}{"title": "C:C is a response option in the context of the que